    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart (1756–1791) composed symphonies, operas, chamber music, and piano works with effortless melodic balance — the epitome of Classical style."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "contributions",
      "title": "Contributions",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Over 600 works including operas *The Marriage of Figaro*, *Don Giovanni*, *The Magic Flute*. Piano concertos and symphonies define Classical form. Child prodigy who toured Europe before age 10."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "phrasing-model",
      "title": "Phrasing model",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Clear four-bar antecedent/consequent structure. Alberti bass and I–V–I motion underpin countless songs. Lift at midpoint cadence, settle at authentic cadence."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "for-trad-players",
      "title": "For trad players",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Mozart's phrasing helps shape airs and slow session tunes with intentional breathing points."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
